43:40.580 --> 43:46.940
So my vector b and my matrix h consists of elements which involve the Jacobian.

43:46.940 --> 43:51.680
So for the H matrix, very clearly you can see the Jacobian popping up twice here, and

43:51.680 --> 43:55.660
also for the B matrix, you see the Jacobian being over here.

43:55.660 --> 44:01.720
So as you will see, the sparse matrix in the Jacobian will also lead to a sparse matrix

44:01.720 --> 44:08.640
H, and this is one of the key reasons why we can actually solve them in an efficient

44:08.640 --> 44:09.640
manner.

