And now we need to see what happens if we actually sum those elements up, so sum H up

46:07.760 --> 46:11.360
and sum b up over all constraints that we have.

46:11.360 --> 46:18.800
So if you take multiple of those vectors together, we will actually see that we get a fully dense

46:18.800 --> 46:19.800
vector b.

46:19.800 --> 46:24.120
