46:26.740 --> 46:28.780
It's however different for my H matrix.

46:28.780 --> 46:33.120
So again, I have n squared elements in here, and always four for every constraint will

46:33.120 --> 46:34.180
be filled.

46:34.180 --> 46:37.720
So by adding all of them up, I will typically get a matrix which looks like this.

46:37.720 --> 46:43.340
So I have direct constraints here on the diagonal, which are the constraints, and also the direct

46:43.340 --> 46:47.820
